%%
%% SECTION 8: SECURITY CONTROLS
%%
\section{Security Controls: Mitigation as Defense in Depth}
\label{sec:controls}

Mitigation research spans the model lifecycle, from curation of preference data through targeted
fine-tuning, inference-time prompting and steering, real-time monitoring, and governance.
Figure~\ref{fig:mitigation} organizes the interventions into four tiers, and
Appendix~\ref{app:mitigations} compares the primary methods on effectiveness, cost, applicability,
mechanism, and trade-offs. Reading them as security controls rather than research prototypes
imposes a discipline the literature mostly lacks: each control must state which channel of the
threat model it addresses, and Table~\ref{tab:coverage} makes that mapping explicit. No single
intervention dominates across sycophancy forms and domains, so deployed assurance must combine
tiers calibrated to context.

\begin{figure}[ht]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{fig_mitigation.pdf}
\caption{Four-tier sycophancy mitigation framework. Tier 1 (data level) addresses the preference
data pipeline; Tier 2 (training level) targets model parameters; Tier 3 (inference level) applies
at deployment time without weight updates; Tier 4 (policy level) provides evaluation standards
and governance. Later tiers complement but do not substitute for earlier-tier fixes.}
\label{fig:mitigation}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Data and Training Tier}
\label{subsec:training}

The most durable interventions act before deployment. Adding synthetic examples in which
sycophantic responses are marked incorrect and truthful but unwelcome responses are marked correct
significantly reduces sycophancy on held-out prompts without degrading general
capability~\citep{wei2023synthetic}, an approach extended to decoder-only architectures
by \citet{wang2024synthetic} and validated independently by Pressure-Tune, which fine-tunes on
synthetic adversarial dialogues paired with chain-of-thought rationales that explicitly reject
user misinformation~\citep{zhang2025pressure}. Precision matters as much as data: Supervised
Pinpoint Tuning identifies the fewer than 5\% of attention heads that drive sycophantic behavior
and fine-tunes only those, yielding a 71.84\% increase in confidence and a 67.83\% increase in
truthfulness on Llama-2-13B with 168 million tunable parameters, where naive supervised
fine-tuning on the same objective costs 8.57\% GSM8K accuracy that SPT instead improves by
1.59\%~\citep{chen2024pinpoint}. CAUSM attributes sycophancy to spurious correlations between user
preference and output and removes them through causally motivated head reweighting and calibration
along the causal direction~\citep{li2025causm}. Constitutional AI embeds honesty norms in the
training objective through self-critique and revision~\citep{bai2022constitutional}, which is more
durable than instructing a deployed model not to be sycophantic. SMART reframes the problem as
reasoning optimization, generating truthful trajectories under pressure with uncertainty-aware
tree search and training on them with reinforcement learning~\citep{beigi2025smart}, consistent
with the independent finding that reasoning-optimized models resist better than alignment-tuned
models of similar size~\citep{hong2025sycon}. Direct Preference Optimization offers a middle path
between these and full RLHF, contrasting sycophantic with truthful completions without a separate
reward model that is itself susceptible to preference bias; its effectiveness depends critically
on curation, since preference corpora overrepresent agreeable responses and must be actively
filtered and augmented with contrastive pairs whose preferred response is factually superior
independent of tone~\citep{wei2023synthetic,wang2024synthetic,chen2024pinpoint}.

\subsection{Inference Tier: Prompting, Steering, Monitoring}
\label{subsec:inference}

Inference-time controls deploy on existing systems without weight updates, exploiting the framing
sensitivity of Section~\ref{subsec:prompt_sensitivity}. Asking the model to convert a user's
assertion into a question before answering cuts sycophancy substantially, more than a system
prompt instructing the model not to be sycophantic, robustly across GPT-4o, GPT-5, and Claude
Sonnet 4.5~\citep{dubois2026askdont}; the user-side variant, guidance to ask rather than assert,
achieves the same effect without model changes. Instructing a neutral third-person perspective
reduces multi-turn sycophancy by up to 63.8\%, with anti-sycophancy system prompts adding a
smaller 28\%, but both degrade as conversations lengthen~\citep{hong2025sycon}, which is exactly
the regime the threat model flags.

White-box access enables steering. Contrastive Activation Addition computes a steering vector from
the mean activation difference between sycophantic and truthful responses and adds it at inference
time, effective over and above prompts and fine-tuning without labeled training
data~\citep{panickssery2023steering}; linear probes in attention activations modulate sycophancy
without degrading factual accuracy and transfer across QA domains~\citep{genadi2026linear}.
Representation editing treats the model as a controllable dynamical system, computing optimal
control signals over the hidden-state trajectory from a Bellman value function, and outperforms
other test-time alignment at a fraction of fine-tuning cost~\citep{kong2024repredit}; the anchor
localization of \citet{duszenko2026anchors} suggests such control could target the specific
generation steps where agreement is committed. For reasoning models, MONICA monitors per-step
drift scores during inference and calibrates away sycophantic drift before it compounds, reducing
sycophancy in both intermediate steps and final answers across 12 datasets and three
models~\citep{hu2025monica}.

\subsection{Governance Tier and Human Oversight}
\label{subsec:policy}

Technical controls persist only if evaluation is institutionalized. Development pipelines should
measure sycophancy the way bias and hallucination are measured, comparing outputs with and without
user-belief context~\citep{fanous2025syceval}, with AEDI providing a scalar suitable for
longitudinal tracking across model versions~\citep{botas2026aedi}. High-stakes deployments should
be required to report multi-turn adversarial results (SYCON, Pressure-Tune) and single-turn
factual audits (SycEval) in model cards and release criteria~\citep{hong2025sycon,
zhang2025pressure,fanous2025syceval}, and scalar metrics such as PARROT follow rates and AEDI are
operationalizable for regulatory oversight~\citep{celebi2025parrot,botas2026aedi}. In sensitive
domains, systems should be restricted from unqualified agreement, with human professional
oversight when input suggests clinical risk.

Oversight obligations follow from the consequence evidence. Sycophancy erodes epistemic autonomy,
shaping beliefs toward the user's priors while raising trust~\citep{turner2026programmed,
cheng2025prosocial,ibrahim2026warm}. Deployers serving vulnerable populations, where safety
interventions currently occur in fewer than one third of delusional-content
turns~\citep{auyeung2025psychogenic} and compliance with clinically false requests reaches
100\%~\citep{chen2025helpfulness}, carry a duty of care to demonstrate sycophancy resistance under
social and authority pressure, not merely to pass static content classifiers. Transparency is the
last layer: users rarely understand that agreement is trained rather than evidentiary, so
disclosures, visible disagreement indicators, and interface guidance are legitimate controls at
the interaction layer.

\subsection{Coverage: Controls Against the Threat Model}
\label{subsec:coverage}

Table~\ref{tab:coverage} crosses the control tiers with the channels of
Section~\ref{sec:threatmodel}. Two structural gaps stand out. First, the premise and
document-supply channel is essentially uncovered: every surveyed control targets deference to the
\emph{user}, while provenance and sanitization of retrieved or embedded content, the prerequisite
identified in Section~\ref{sec:injection}, has no dedicated mitigation in the sycophancy
literature; injection defenses form an adjacent literature with partly different controls, and a
deployment facing both failure modes needs both. Second, covert sycophancy is unmeasured and therefore unmitigated: no control is
validated against displacement into selective framing or evidence weighting
(Section~\ref{subsec:appraisal}), so every full circle in the overt columns overstates assurance
against the covert variant. A third, softer conclusion is that the strongest cells depend on white-box
access or retraining, leaving deployments built on closed third-party APIs with only the weakest
tier, prompting plus monitoring.

